module nupp.foreign

--[[
C callbacks a program keeps past the call it passes them to.

A Nupp function passed to a `cdef` function-pointer parameter is lent a
trampoline for that call alone: C that keeps the pointer and calls it after the
call returns is refused. `retain` makes a callback C may keep. It passes wherever
the function would and Nupp may call it as the function; its C signature is that
of the first parameter it is passed to, and passing it to a parameter of another
signature is refused. `rebind` changes what it calls without changing the
pointer C holds, and `release` ends it: C calling the pointer afterwards is
refused rather than reaching freed code.

The handle is untyped: the `cdef` parameter it is passed to is what checks the
function's type against the C signature.

C calls a callback on the VM's own thread, inside a native call that VM made. A
call from any other thread returns zero to C and raises once the native call in
flight, or the next one, returns.
]]

local native = require("nupp.vm.foreign")

local foreign = {}

--- Retains `f` as a C callback until `release`.
function foreign.retain(f: any): any
    return native.callback(nil, f)
end

--- Makes a retained callback call `f`; the pointer C holds does not change.
--- @raises string when `callback` is not a retained callback or was released.
function foreign.rebind(callback: any, f: any): nil
    native.setCallback(callback, f)
end

--- Releases a retained callback. C calling it afterwards is refused.
function foreign.release(callback: any): nil
    native.close(callback)
end

export = foreign
